					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/soullesssingularity" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(637830); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=637830&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1605970069" alt="SoullessSingularity" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=637830)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/soullesssingularity" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(637830); return false;" >SoullessSingularity</a></span> <span class="odate time_1397929592 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">19 Apr 2014 17:46</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2015340">
									

<p>This mostly all started because a newbie asked me to help them do the story part of storytelling, to which I realized I only have my personal method to recommend and I found it terribly inadequate. Also around that time there was a bit of debate as to how newbies should be introduced to the Foundation's tone, variety of article, etc.</p>
<p>This will be a living document, meaning people will be added (or removed if necessary) and accounts can be edited as the authors refine and change their styles.</p>
<p>I'd like to thank everyone that has contributed and look forward to further contributions!</p>

							</div>

										<div class="signature">
					<hr class="signature-separator"/>
					

<p>Living the dream, or dreaming the life?</p>

